target:    src/Schema/Schema.php
gate:      php tests/schema-single-source-test.php
kind:      restore-defect
expect:    Schema::engine() does not return InnoDB
rationale: C42 as it actually shipped: `SHOW VARIABLES LIKE 'have_innodb'` was removed in MySQL 5.6.1, so the probe answered empty on every modern server and the ENGINE clause was dropped from all three CREATE TABLEs. The tables took the host default; on a MyISAM host the slim_events FOREIGN KEY is silently ignored, and Phase G's migration hard-refuses MyISAM — so v6 would refuse to migrate an install v6 itself created. This mutation reproduces the OUTCOME (a non-InnoDB engine) rather than the removed probe, because the outcome is what a user experiences and the probe is only one way to reach it.
---
diff --git a/src/Schema/Schema.php b/src/Schema/Schema.php
index fc961104..966a28d2 100644
--- a/src/Schema/Schema.php
+++ b/src/Schema/Schema.php
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ final class Schema
     /**
      * Unconditional. See C42 in the class docblock — this is the whole fix.
      */
-    public const ENGINE = 'InnoDB';
+    public const ENGINE = '';
 
     /**
      * Used when `wp_users.user_login` cannot be inspected — an external-DB install where the
